{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1415929-assistance-sought-for-a-capstone-evocation","id":1415929,"title":"Assistance Sought for a Capstone Evocation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-09-28T20:28:57-07:00","id":1415929,"title":"Assistance Sought for a Capstone Evocation","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><span style=\"font-family:georgia, serif\">Here's the writeup to date. General feedback on the Evocations is also accepted.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:BlackChancery\">Verdant Springwood (Artifact \u2022\u2022\u2022 Jade Powerbow)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Verdant Springwood was carved during the Shogunate for the Busujima Clan, later than Ebony Fronds, for use by Shutaro\u2019s eldest son, Mamoru. Carved from a yew tree allowed to fall of age and storm, it was lacquered with the sap of a lacquer tree mixed with a small amount of green jade, then after several coats, the words \u201cthe Green gives life and takes it away\u201d painted on it in green, then more coats of lacquer. The bow, like the armour, was for a long time, used in time of war and left in the rain and sun in time of pierce. In due course, it passed into the hands of other sons, and less often daughters, of the Clan. As with their other great treasures, the Clan took great pride in knowing that they had never had to ransom it back from their enemies. After the clan\u2019s destruction, it passed into the hands of Saeko Takagi, their former retainer and recently Exalted Dawn Caste.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">The bow contains a single hearthstone socket, currently empty. So long as sufficient suitable plant life is available, such as brambles, branches or vines, the attuned wielder need only set a piece to the bow for it to become an arrow, and therefore will not run out of ammunition.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:BlackChancery\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Evocations of Verdant Springwood</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#01A815\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Eye of the Forest</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Cost</b>: 3m; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Type</b>: Supplemental</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Keywords</b>: Dissonant, Resonant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Duration</b>: Indefinite</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisites</b>: None</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">The wielder of Verdant Springwood is as one with the Green. This Evocation enhances Awareness rolls made while in a forest, jungle, or other vegetation-dense terrain, lowering any penalties by the wielder\u2019s (Essence).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Special activation rules</b>: As long as the wearer isn\u2019t dissonant with jade, this Evocation awakens at no cost when the bow is first is attuned and drawn in a forest, jungle, or similar.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Resonant</b>: This Evocation also reduces the benefit of plant-based cover to the wielder\u2019s targets by the wielder\u2019s (Essence).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#01A815\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Hunter\u2019s Blind</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Cost</b>: 2m; <b>Mins</b>: Essence 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Type</b>: Supplemental</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Keywords</b>: None</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Duration</b>: Indefinite</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisites</b>: Eye of the Forest, Invisible Statue Spirit</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">The greatest advantage an archer can have is concealment, and this Evocation provides that. So long as the wielder is in an area dominated by vegetation such as a forest or a jungle, the wielder can use Verdant Springwood to launch ranged attacks without losing the benefit of Invisible Statue Spirit.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#01A815\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Poison in Every Part</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Cost:</b> 3m<b> Mins</b>: Essence 1</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Type</b>: Supplemental</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Keywords</b>: Decisive-Only, Resonant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Duration</b>: Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisites</b>: None</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">The main defence of many plants is poison, and this Evocation reflects that truth. If a decisive attack inflicts at least one health level, the target suffers the following poison effect:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">(wielder\u2019s Essence)i/round (L in crash) (wielder\u2019s Essence) rounds (wielder\u2019s Essence)</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Those who are not resonant with jade cannot awaken this Evocation.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#01A815\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Poison Against Poison</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Cost:</b> 5m<b> Mins</b>: Essence 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Type</b>: Supplemental</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Keywords</b>: None</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Duration</b>: Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\"><b>Prerequisites</b>: Poison in Every Part</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">With this Evocation, the archer can draw an arrow and infuse it with a toxin that has properties opposed to whatever afflicts the target (which must be determined by diagnosis). The poison from which the target suffers loses (archer\u2019s Essence) from its penalty and its remaining duration; an Essence 2 archer, for example, would reduce arrow frog venom damage to 0i/0L and its remaining duration by 2 rounds. The arrow itself inflicts a level of lethal damage.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-28T22:33:55-07:00","id":1415944,"title":"","content":"Ok so, on the whole, I like it. I get the theme right away and its easy to see what kind of character this is for. <br /> <br /> Eye of the Forest is good but also a little weak. I'd have it eliminate the penalties all together and make the Resonant ability something greater, like the ability to make awareness checks at no penalty out to extreme range. <br /> <br /> I really don't like Hunter's Blind and evocations that rely on a specific charm to use. The idea is sound, attacking without breaking stealth, but I'd change the effect to be charm-neutral. <br /> <br /> The 2 poison charms are kind of weird. The first two charms are about being a silent forest hunter and the second two are about being a poison plant. The backstory said this is a Yew and Lacquer bow, neither of those are poisonous. <br /> <br /> Im not an expert on poison damage but Poisonbin Every Part looks too good. For one, there's no restriction on spilling blood or distance so if you get shot by another archer they just get magically poisoned. Or a storm witch hits you with lightning. Also there's no save. <br /> <br /> Poison Against Poison seems like a medical charm, which is cool flavor but bad execution. First theres no info about how to properly diagnose a poison, and you have to lethally shoot whoever is poisoned. What scenario is this for? I'd make this a benefit of the bow itself, like it produces an acorn at dawn that can nullify 1 mundane poison. Make the acorns lose power after a day so they cant be stockpiled. <br /> <br /> Im not sure if the &quot;shoot branches&quot; effect should be an evocation or not, but its cool flavor and I love Akutagawa so go for it. <br /> <br /> I don't know what youre looking for in a capstone, theres 2 &quot;flavors&quot; here and I don't know if you wanna mix them. <br /> <br /> You dont have an arrow that poisons people. You dont have a bonus to stealth in the woods. Presumably this is for a hunter/forest warrior but there's nothing about tracking prey. A charm that lets you cause plants to make difficult terrain wouldnt be amiss either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Please be warned: this is not champagne, this is most likely a duck.<br /> -<i>Chausse</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#800080\"><i>Message me for Japanese translations.</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8830-sorcerous-overlord","name":"Sorcerous Overlord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8830_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-29T06:19:38-07:00","id":1415962,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Here's a rewrite of Poison in Every Part: The main defence of many plants is poison, and this Evocation reflects that truth. If a decisive attack using Verdant Springwood inflicts at least one health level, the target suffers the following poison effect:</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:11px\">Oh, and some </span></span><span style=\"font-size:11px\">lacquers are toxic.</span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">Concerning &quot;Poison Against Poison,&quot; the intent of it is for use against stronger toxins, where it's a case of &quot;injured is better than dead.&quot; Diagnosis rules are already in the main book under Medicine, and I saw no need to include those rules here.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1184,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","user":"LadyLens","date":". 09-29-2020, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}